{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzTaQPBuYya1ZS8a2naE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BKRVi7ZmF9PgkPzmeuk6QD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\godle\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\jd-live-02dfjj_z\\project\\docs\\checkout-flow.md","content":"# Checkout flow: placing an order\n\nSequence of `place_order()` in `src/app.py`, with the card charge from `src/payments.py`.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Client\n    participant App as app.place_order\n    participant Stock as STOCK (in memory)\n    participant Pay as payments.charge\n    participant File as data/orders.json\n\n    Client->>App: place_order(customer, items, card_token)\n\n    loop each item in items\n        App->>Stock: STOCK.get(name, 0) vs qty\n        Note right of Stock: unknown item counts as 0 stock\n    end\n\n    alt any item short on stock\n        App-->>Client: rejected, out of stock: name\n    else all items in stock\n        App->>Pay: charge(card_token, total(items))\n        Note right of App: total = PRICES x qty, in cents\n        Pay-->>App: {ok, id}\n\n        alt payment not ok (or no card_token)\n            App-->>Client: rejected, payment failed\n        else payment ok\n            App->>Stock: decrement STOCK by qty\n            Note right of Stock: after charge, no lock\n            App->>File: read orders.json (or [] if missing)\n            App->>App: order = id len+1, customer, items, payment id\n            App->>File: write orders.json with new order\n            App-->>Client: placed, order\n        end\n    end\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Stock is checked before payment, but decremented after it.** Nothing reserves stock during the charge, so two concurrent orders can both pass the check.\n- **Stock lives only in memory.** `STOCK` resets to its hard-coded values on restart and is never written to `orders.json`.\n- **Failure after charge loses the order.** If the file write fails after `charge` succeeds, the card is charged but no order is recorded. Stock is also already decremented.\n- **`charge` ignores the amount.** It returns `ok` for any non-empty token and never reads `amount_cents`. It never raises.\n- **Order IDs come from the file length.** `id = len(orders) + 1`, so IDs are not safe under concurrent writes.\n- **Docs mismatch.** The README mentions `POST /orders` and an email receipt. Neither exists in `src/`: there is no HTTP route and no email code.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1428,"cache_read_input_tokens":39205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1428},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c0145fc-0180-4352-99fa-79e7e8c491c0","uuid":"1bc64411-c679-43b4-8d26-44bc9642b75d","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:32:19.153Z","request_id":"req_011CgzTaQA2s2mPczY3vQkbi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BKRVi7ZmF9PgkPzmeuk6QD":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\godle\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\jd-live-02dfjj_z\\project\\docs\\checkout-flow.md","content":"# Checkout flow: placing an order\n\nSequence of `place_order()` in `src/app.py`, with the card charge from `src/payments.py`.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Client\n    participant App as app.place_order\n    participant Stock as STOCK (in memory)\n    participant Pay as payments.charge\n    participant File as data/orders.json\n\n    Client->>App: place_order(customer, items, card_token)\n\n    loop each item in items\n        App->>Stock: STOCK.get(name, 0) vs qty\n        Note right of Stock: unknown item counts as 0 stock\n    end\n\n    alt any item short on stock\n        App-->>Client: rejected, out of stock: name\n    else all items in stock\n        App->>Pay: charge(card_token, total(items))\n        Note right of App: total = PRICES x qty, in cents\n        Pay-->>App: {ok, id}\n\n        alt payment not ok (or no card_token)\n            App-->>Client: rejected, payment failed\n        else payment ok\n            App->>Stock: decrement STOCK by qty\n            Note right of Stock: after charge, no lock\n            App->>File: read orders.json (or [] if missing)\n            App->>App: order = id len+1, customer, items, payment id\n            App->>File: write orders.json with new order\n            App-->>Client: placed, order\n        end\n    end\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Stock is checked before payment, but decremented after it.** Nothing reserves stock during the charge, so two concurrent orders can both pass the check.\n- **Stock lives only in memory.** `STOCK` resets to its hard-coded values on restart and is never written to `orders.json`.\n- **Failure after charge loses the order.** If the file write fails after `charge` succeeds, the card is charged but no order is recorded. Stock is also already decremented.\n- **`charge` ignores the amount.** It returns `ok` for any non-empty token and never reads `amount_cents`. It never raises.\n- **Order IDs come from the file length.** `id = len(orders) + 1`, so IDs are not safe under concurrent writes.\n- **Docs mismatch.** The README mentions `POST /orders` and an email receipt. Neither exists in `src/`: there is no HTTP route and no email code.\n"}}}
